  "details": "I was making an Avatar where the Cube was 1mx1mx1m had a View Position 500 Meters Above the Model and it was fine no matter where I put it but when I change the Z Axis to be even 5 Meters Behind It, the avatar automatically switches it to the center since it was behind the model, I can't do it in front either. I was trying to have it 1000 Meters behind the Model but it still switches to the center when I was Trying to have it Behind The Model On Purpose. The Cube does not have Any Rig at all so why won't it let me do it no matter what I do. I put the cube behind the object, elongated it to be 500m long wirh the Z Axis at 500m behind the GameObject and even moved the Game Object with the Z Position and It still puts it in The Exact Middle where I don't want it to be. Is there anything I can do to Move the Z Axis for the Cube to be Behind or In Front of the Actual Model? (2022 SDK)",
